            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.069,
            0.488,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.108,
            0.885,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For factoring "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 } + 8 x + 1 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we need a and b such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + b = 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a b = 1 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.149,
            0.885,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a \\; = \\; 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and b = 5 is one possibility. The possible length and breadth of Saira’s rectangle in terms of x are: length = x + 5 units and breadth "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= x + 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.207,
            0.656,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now draw Saira’s rectangle using these pieces."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.232,
            0.885,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 18:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A rectangular pool is such that its breadth is 4 metres less than its length and its area is 96 sq. metres. Find the length and breadth of the pool."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.29,
            0.884,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let the length of the pool be x metres. Then the breadth of the pool is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " metres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.329,
            0.821,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since the area is given to be 96 sq. metres, we get x(x – 4) = 96."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.352,
            0.677,
            0.371
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "x^{2}-4x=96\\mathrm{~or~}x^{2}-4x-96=0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.377,
            0.884,
            0.417
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We choose appropriate factors of – 96 to split the term –4x. We know that, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-12) \\times 8 = 96   and   (-12) + 8 = -4."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Hence – 4x can be written as –12x + 8x ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.423,
            0.878,
            0.442
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_20_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "x^{2}-4x-96=x^{2}-12x+8x-96=x(x-12)+8(x-12)=(x-12)(x+8)=0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.449,
            0.698,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x^{2}-4x-96=0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " implies that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(x - 12)(x + 8) = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.475,
            0.58,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means either "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - 12 = 0 \\\\ 0 \\bar{x} + 8 = 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.499,
            0.886,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, x = 12 or x = –8. Since x is the length of the pool, it cannot be negative. Therefore, we ignore x = –8 and x = 12 metres must be the length of the pool. The breadth of the pool "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - 4 = 12 - 4 = 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " metres."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.585,
            0.692,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "End-of-Chapter Exercises"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.633,
            0.763,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Use suitable identities to find the following products: (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(-3x + 4)^{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( 2 s + 7 \\right) \\left( 2 s - 7 \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left(p^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(p^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 2 n + 7 )   ( 2 n - 7 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (v) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(s - 2t)\\left(s^{2} + 2st + 4t^{2}\\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (vi) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\frac { 1 } { 2 r } }   -   4 r \\right) ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (vii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( - 3 m + 4 k - l ) ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (viii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( x   -   { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } y \\right) ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ix) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\frac { 7 } { 2 } } k   -   { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } m \\right) ^ { 3 }"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
